<zk xmlns:n="native">
	<style>
		/* A wrap-mode badge indicator is pulled 10px outside the box of the child it
		   decorates. .z-hlayout sets overflow:hidden, so an hlayout cuts that overhang
		   off - see the Wrap mode section, which uses this row instead. */
		.badge-wrap-row { display: flex; gap: 30px; align-items: center; padding: 12px 0; }
	</style>

	<n:h1>Inline mode</n:h1>
	a standalone badge with no children renders at the document position
	<n:h2>Value</n:h2>
	<badge value="NEW"/>
	<n:h2>Count and max</n:h2>
	count above max (default 99) renders as {max}+
	<badge count="5"/>
	<badge count="120"/>
	<badge count="8" max="5"/>
	<n:h2>Value takes precedence over count</n:h2>
	a non-null value wins; the count is ignored
	<badge value="HOT" count="42"/>
	<n:h2>Show zero</n:h2>
	by default a zero count renders nothing; showZero forces it
	<badge count="0"/>
	<badge count="0" showZero="true"/>
	<n:h2>Empty rendering</n:h2>
	with dot="false", no value, a zero count and showZero="false", a badge renders no
	indicator at all: the element stays in the DOM but collapses to zero size, so the
	three badges below are invisible
	<badge/>
	<badge count="0"/>
	<badge value=""/>
	<n:h2>Severity</n:h2>
	<badge count="1" severity="info"/>
	<badge count="2" severity="success"/>
	<badge count="3" severity="warning"/>
	<badge count="4" severity="danger"/>
	<badge count="5" severity="secondary"/>

	<n:h1>Wrap mode</n:h1>
	with exactly one child, the badge overlays the child at the given placement.
	The indicator is pulled 10px past the corner of the child, so the container has to
	let it overflow - an hlayout clips it and the indicator loses its top or bottom edge.
	The row below is a div styled with flex and a gap, which keeps the overhang visible
	and also keeps two neighbouring badges from overlapping.
	<div sclass="badge-wrap-row">
		<badge count="3" placement="top_right">
			<button label="Inbox"/>
		</badge>
		<badge count="7" placement="top_left">
			<button label="Alerts"/>
		</badge>
		<badge count="9" placement="bottom_right">
			<button label="Tasks"/>
		</badge>
		<badge count="2" placement="bottom_left">
			<button label="Drafts"/>
		</badge>
	</div>

	<n:h1>Dot</n:h1>
	the dot mode ignores value/count and shows a small colored dot
	<badge dot="true" severity="danger" placement="top_right">
		<button label="Messages"/>
	</badge>
	<n:h2>Dot severity</n:h2>
	severity still drives the dot color
	<badge dot="true" severity="info"/>
	<badge dot="true" severity="success"/>
	<badge dot="true" severity="warning"/>
	<badge dot="true" severity="danger"/>
	<badge dot="true" severity="secondary"/>

	<n:h1>Live update</n:h1>
	setCount/setValue re-render the badge, including the transition to and from empty
	<badge id="liveBadge" count="0" placement="top_right">
		<button label="Approvals"/>
	</badge>
	<hlayout>
		<button label="+1">
			<attribute name="onClick">
				liveBadge.setCount(liveBadge.getCount() + 1);
			</attribute>
		</button>
		<button label="-1">
			<attribute name="onClick">
				liveBadge.setCount(Math.max(0, liveBadge.getCount() - 1));
			</attribute>
		</button>
		<label id="displayValue" value="getDisplayValue():"/>
		<button label="Read getDisplayValue()">
			<attribute name="onClick">
				displayValue.setValue("getDisplayValue(): [" + liveBadge.getDisplayValue() + "]");
			</attribute>
		</button>
	</hlayout>

	<n:h1>Use Cases</n:h1>

	<n:h2>Sidebar navigation counters</n:h2>
	each menu entry carries its own pending workload; the cap keeps a long queue from
	widening the sidebar
	<vlayout style="border:1px solid #ddd; border-radius:4px; padding:12px; width:260px">
		<hlayout valign="middle">
			<label value="Inbox" hflex="1"/>
			<badge count="12" severity="info"/>
		</hlayout>
		<hlayout valign="middle">
			<label value="Pending approvals" hflex="1"/>
			<badge count="4" severity="warning"/>
		</hlayout>
		<hlayout valign="middle">
			<label value="Failed imports" hflex="1"/>
			<badge count="128" max="99" severity="danger"/>
		</hlayout>
		<hlayout valign="middle">
			<label value="Archive" hflex="1"/>
			<badge count="0"/>
		</hlayout>
	</vlayout>

	<n:h2>Notification bell</n:h2>
	the dot says "something is new" without committing to a number
	<toolbar>
		<badge dot="true" severity="danger" placement="top_right">
			<toolbarbutton iconSclass="z-icon-bell" tooltiptext="Notifications"/>
		</badge>
		<badge dot="true" severity="info" placement="top_right">
			<toolbarbutton iconSclass="z-icon-envelope" tooltiptext="Messages"/>
		</badge>
	</toolbar>

	<n:h2>Order status column</n:h2>
	the status text of each row is mapped to a severity so the state is readable at a glance
	<grid width="520px">
		<columns>
			<column label="Order" width="140px"/>
			<column label="Customer"/>
			<column label="Status" width="150px"/>
		</columns>
		<rows>
			<row>
				<label value="SO-2026-0913"/>
				<label value="ACME Industrial"/>
				<badge value="NEW" severity="info"/>
			</row>
			<row>
				<label value="SO-2026-0914"/>
				<label value="Northwind Traders"/>
				<badge value="SHIPPED" severity="success"/>
			</row>
			<row>
				<label value="SO-2026-0915"/>
				<label value="Globex Corp"/>
				<badge value="ON HOLD" severity="warning"/>
			</row>
			<row>
				<label value="SO-2026-0916"/>
				<label value="Initech"/>
				<badge value="PAYMENT FAILED" severity="danger"/>
			</row>
		</rows>
	</grid>

	<n:h2>Toolbar counters that vanish at zero</n:h2>
	an empty queue renders no badge at all, so a clean toolbar means there is nothing to do
	<toolbar>
		<badge count="3" placement="top_right">
			<toolbarbutton label="Import queue"/>
		</badge>
		<badge count="0" placement="top_right">
			<toolbarbutton label="Export queue"/>
		</badge>
		<badge count="0" showZero="true" severity="secondary" placement="top_right">
			<toolbarbutton label="Reconciliation"/>
		</badge>
	</toolbar>
</zk>
